WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.729
Film Courage: Did you approach Issa Rae about
KING ESTER [webseries] or did she approach

00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:04.729
you?

00:00:04.729 --> 00:00:08.099
Dui Jarrod, Writer/Director: The producer
Caralene Robinson she had approached Deniese

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:15.799
Davis over there who is kind of Issa’s right
hand.

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:21.260
They were the first people that we had connected
with about KING ESTER but at the time they

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.691
were trying to do some new things digitally,
we hadn’t really gotten out on the film

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.800
festival circuit and so we just kind of had
a meeting of the minds.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.200
It was nice that when it came back around
and we had looked at all the options on the

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.830
table we chose the option that we had kind
of found from the very beginning which was

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.420
Issa Rae’s production company.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.550
Film Courage: Sorry, it was already finished?

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.220
Dui: It was already finished.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.470
Even when we initially caught up with them,
we had sent them the version of KING ESTER

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:55.380
and they really, really loved it and saw the
value of it but they weren’t ready to release

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.030
on their network or anything like that at
that time.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:03.190
And then we came back later everything was
just beautifully aligned for us to work together

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.190
on it.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.870
Film Courage: And KING ESTER is about what?

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:11.630
Dui: KING ESTER is a short form digital content
series about a transgender woman in New Orleans

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:18.980
7 days before Hurricane Katrina and her decision
to either stay or leave as the hurricane comes

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.920
to town.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.450
Each episode is for one day in her life

